        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7352080?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This change addresses the dev-docs-needed requirement of <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1773681\" rel=\"nofollow\">Bug 1773681</a> Enable showing \"Paste\" button for <code class=\"notranslate\">navigator.clipboard.readText()</code> when called from Addons which don't have <code class=\"notranslate\">clipboardRead</code> permssion.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The changes include:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>a release note.</li>\n<li>an update to the Interact with the clipboard article. In addition to aligning the documentation with this change, references to the deprecated <code class=\"notranslate\">document.execCommand</code> methods were removed.</li>\n<li>an update to the clipboard section on the Pesmissions page to remove references to the deprecated <code class=\"notranslate\">document.execCommand</code> methods.</li>\n<li>an update to the Clipboard API overview page's Security consideration section to align the documentation with this change.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Notes in the BCD updated in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3699897493\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/28587\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28587/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28587\">mdn/browser-compat-data#28587</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42263",
            "title": "Bug-1773681 Showing Paste button for navigator.clipboard.readText()",
            "date_modified": "2025-12-08T19:59:16.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-12-05T18:04:47.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "rebloor",
                "url": "https://github.com/rebloor"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45551?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Adds translations for the mdn-data-free version of rari. Existing translations on the formal definition values cannot be carried over, so there is a new translations file with only en-US values pre-filled and the rest auto-translated for a baseline.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Remove mdn-data dependency from the publishing pipeline.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This is compatible with the old and the new approach to formal definitions. Before merging the rari-part of this, nothing will change on the output.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">See related rari PR: <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3652539630\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/rari/issues/390\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/rari/pull/390/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/rari/pull/390\">mdn/rari#390</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42241",
            "title": "Translations for css formal definitions",
            "date_modified": "2025-12-08T13:52:36.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-12-05T10:33:37.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "argl",
                "url": "https://github.com/argl"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/100893747?u=5c736b1b891889a78840dca35835b9f488a45072&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This PR updates the </p><details> element documentation to reflect modern animation support.<br>\nThe outdated text claiming that transitions cannot be animated has been replaced with updated guidance referencing ::details-content, which enables smooth animations as part of Baseline since September 2025.<br>\nDuplicate sentences were also removed for clarity.<p dir=\"auto\"></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">💡 Motivation</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Developers reading MDN were misled into believing that </p><details> cannot animate opens/closes.<br>\nThis change ensures the documentation is accurate and helps readers understand how to animate <details> widgets using the new pseudo-element.<p dir=\"auto\"></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">🔗 Related Issue</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #42226.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3694297894\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42226\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/42226/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42226\">#42226</a></p></details></details></details>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42239",
            "title": "Docs: update <details> animation docs to reference ::details-content (#42226)",
            "date_modified": "2025-12-08T11:35:45.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-12-05T07:17:42.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "Khogendrarupini",
                "url": "https://github.com/Khogendrarupini"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"http://localhost:5042/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document/execCommand#commandname\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">Document.execCommand()</code></a> with command <code class=\"notranslate\">insertHTML</code> is an injection sink.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Given that this is just a small part of what the method does, and that the method is deprecated, I have added the disclaimer to the point where <code class=\"notranslate\">insertHTML</code> is documented. The disclaimer does not link to a security considerations section, but instead points to the TT API overview. I think this is the right level.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Project tracking in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3510273732\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41507\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/41507/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41507\">#41507</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42238",
            "title": "TrustedTypes: Document.execCommand() with command insertHTML",
            "date_modified": "2025-12-05T06:15:51.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-12-05T06:13:57.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 131 supports the <a href=\"https://drafts.csswg.org/css-anchor-position-1/#anchor-scope\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">anchor-scope</code></a> property; see <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5094192052436992\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5094192052436992</a>. It is also supported in Safari 26, and behind a pref in Fx Nightly.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR documents <code class=\"notranslate\">anchor-scope</code>.</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #39295.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3023321116\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/39295\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/39295/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/39295\">#39295</a></p>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42227",
            "title": "Editorial review: Document anchor-scope property",
            "date_modified": "2025-12-08T15:42:27.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-12-04T12:30:43.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71914071?u=4a666bc96d47dc4ea33cd16b3b4a2a500047e948&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR updates the Element.scrollTo() page to clarify that:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">scrollTo()</code> is an alias for <code class=\"notranslate\">Element.scroll()</code>.</li>\n<li>Invoking <code class=\"notranslate\">scrollTo()</code> behaves identically to <code class=\"notranslate\">scroll()</code>.</li>\n<li>Added a cross-link to the scroll() page for clarity</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #42222.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3691206082\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42222\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/42222/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42222\">#42222</a></p>\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42223",
            "title": "Clarify that scrollTo() is an alias of scroll()",
            "date_modified": "2025-12-04T04:59:58.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-12-04T04:49:01.000Z",
